      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>This record refers to the work often transmitted under the title
               <t:foreign xml:lang="gez">Sayfa Śǝllāse</t:foreign> that consists of prayers for each day of the week. 
               It can be transmitted without miracles, but is often
                part of the collection <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2286ZenaSellase">Zenā nagaromu la-Śǝllāse</t:ref> in which the prayers for each
               day are followed
            each by a miracle of the Trinity. 
            This work is transmitted for example in <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/SACEth002">Cairo, Société d’Archéologie Copte, Éthiopien 002</t:ref>,
               <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ANLcr53">Rome, Biblioteca dell’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei, Conti Rossini 53</t:ref> or <t:ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/GAet10">Grottaferrata, Exarchic Greek Abbey of St. Mary of Grottaferrata, Crypt. Aet. 10</t:ref>.
            The identification of several recensions of this work or of works with a 
            similar structure but different textual content might be possible in the future.</t:p>
            <t:p>This work is different from <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2281Trinity">Taʾammǝra Śǝllāse</t:ref> (a collection of miracles of the Trinity attributed
               to <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS2748BeduaA">Bǝḍuʿa ʾAmlāk</t:persName>) and from <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2282Trinity">Taʾammǝra Śǝllāse</t:ref> (a collection of miracles of the 
               Trinity transmitted with <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1300Dersan">Dǝrsāna Śǝllāse</t:ref>).
               It is also different from <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT7331SaySelColl">Sayfa Śǝllāse-type collection</t:ref>, a collection also arranged according to the days of the week,
               whose prayers however correspond to <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4691Prayer">Prayer for the weekdays</t:ref>.
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
